What does this program print?

void bump(int n) {
    n = n + 1;
}

int main(void) {
    int a = 5;
    bump(a);
    printf("%d\n", a);
    return 0;
}

This version of max changes its parameter:

int max(int x, int y) {
    int bigger;
    bigger = x;
    if (y > x) {
        bigger = y;
        x = y;
    }
    printf("  in max, before return x: %d y: %d\n", x, y);
    return bigger;
}

main calls res = max(a, b); with a = 13 and b = 100. What value of x does max print?
